/* Loft theme "latte" — Dolphin's Qt style sheet, generated by `loft theme render`, do not edit.
 *
 * Passed by the dolphin launcher programs.loft.qt installs
 * (`dolphin -stylesheet <state>/current/dolphin.qss`): a style sheet is the
 * only way to inset the Places panel's rows. Its delegate (KIO's
 * KFilePlacesViewDelegate) paints each row across the whole viewport, the
 * icon 4 px in, and Kvantum gives dock widgets no content margin, so the
 * padding moves the viewport itself: rows and their selection / hover pills
 * sit 10 px inside the sidebar, like Nautilus's (`margin: 1px 10px`).
 * The style sheet would paint the panel opaque; `background: transparent`
 * keeps the glass (Kvantum's window element) showing through. */
KFilePlacesView {
  padding: 4px 10px 4px 10px;
  background: transparent;
}
KFilePlacesView > QWidget#qt_scrollarea_viewport {
  background: transparent;
}
